# Dhan API Compliance

## Authoritative Sources (in order)

1. `dhan-api-docs.md` in this repo (local export — check here first)
2. https://docs.dhanhq.co/api/v2/
3. https://dhanhq.co/docs/v2/

Never guess endpoints, headers, field names, or auth flows. Read the docs before writing or changing any Dhan integration code.

## Required Practices

- Use exact base URLs, paths, and headers from the docs (e.g. `access-token` header, not `Authorization: Bearer`)
- Match documented request/response field names exactly (`exchangeTradeId`, `tradedQuantity`, `exchangeTime`, etc.)
- This project is **read-only**: Trade History, Holdings, Profile only — no order placement/modification/cancellation
- Static IP whitelisting is **not required** for read-only statement APIs
- Auth: TOTP via `POST https://auth.dhan.co/app/generateAccessToken` with `dhanClientId`, `pin`, `totp`
- Trade History pagination: `GET /trades/{from-date}/{to-date}/{page-number}` starting at page `0`; do not assume termination fields — implement defensively from actual responses

## APIs for This Project

| Purpose | Endpoint |
|---------|----------|
| Auth sanity check | `GET /profile` |
| Primary data source | `GET /trades/{from-date}/{to-date}/{page-number}` |
| Reconciliation only | `GET /holdings` |

Trade History is the authoritative event stream. Holdings is for reconciliation, not historical ledger reconstruction.

## When Docs Are Unclear

Stop and verify against `dhan-api-docs.md` or the official URLs. Do not invent fields, endpoints, or behavior. Phase 0/1 exists to validate real API responses before building business logic.
